// [BUILTIN-ITER-FUSION] The `map`/`filter` stages of a pipeline exist only
// while the function that built it is compiled. Returning the pipeline would
// hand the caller the bare range, so `forEach` would print every number and
// the filter would vanish without a diagnostic.
fn evens(n) = filter(range(0, n), fn(i) => (i % 2) == 0)
fn main() = forEach(evens(6), print)
